WEBVTT

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:11.680
بِسْمِ اللَّهِ  وَالصَّلاةُ وَالسَّلامُ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللهِ وَعَلَى آلِهِ

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.960
وَصَحْبِهِ اَجْمَعِينَ ثُمَّ اَمَّا بَعْدُ

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:18.370
أَمْ أَبْرَمُوٓاْ أَمْرًا فَإِنَّا مُبْرِمُونَ

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:21.200
أَمْ أَبْرَمُوٓاْ أَمْرًا فَإِنَّا مُبْرِمُونَ

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:25.050
The word that repeats itself here is Abrama (ابرم)

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:26.450
Abrama (ابرم)

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.960
Very interesting word of the Arabic language.

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:32.659
You know, nowadays when we do construction

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:33.950
engineering,

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:38.490
then the way we hold a building together is by beams and columns,

00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:40.480
steel columns, concrete columns,

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:43.350
things like that that-- pillars that hold the building up.

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:47.140
And the thing that holds the beams together is

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:49.440
either you weld them together or you yeah--

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.330
either you weld them together or you put

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:52.550
you know, concrete

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.760
or you nail them into each other things like that.

00:00:56.540 --> 00:01:01.280
But in old times, the way they did construction is they took two beams

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:03.050
and they tied them together.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.570
So they would take a really strong kind of rope.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:11.060
And one beam is literally tied to the other beam with a rope.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:13.660
Now, because this is construction,

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:16.790
do you think that that kind of rope or that tying is

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:19.560
a strong kind of tying or a weak kind of tying?

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:23.150
It's strong because it can cause death if you don't do it carefully.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:26.820
So what they do is they take a rope and they they

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.860
take a rope and they double it and they twist it,

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:30.860
so then it becomes stronger.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:35.960
Then they wrap it each way, twice this way, twice this way, twice this way,

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:36.710
twice that way.

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:39.650
And then they tie it so that it's super strong. It doesn't come apart.

00:01:40.481 --> 00:01:42.140
Now what I'm trying to say, then,

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:46.800
is the word Abrama has to do with tying the knot. Literally in Arabic

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:50.560
it has to do with tying a knot, but there's a difference between tying your shoes

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:52.730
and tying a knot for construction.

00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:54.750
When you're tying your shoes, you're going to undo it.

00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:58.400
When you're tying your knot, the knot for construction, it's set.

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:03.050
It's like part of construction. It's a done deal. It should not come off.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.660
It should under no circumstances should this be undone.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:11.160
So this word was used for tying things for permanent purposes,

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:13.860
and the Qur'an uses it

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:18.960
to describe or ask a question about the people who do Shirk; the people of Makkah

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:20.350
the Quraysh.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:24.720
Allah asks a rhetorical question about them, and He asked the question:

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:26.740
أَمْ أَبْرَمُوٓاْ أَمْرًا

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:29.760
Have they tied the knot when it comes to the decision?

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:31.300
What does that mean?

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:35.260
Have the Mushrikun made a final decision that they will not accept Islam?

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:38.320
Have they made a final decision

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:42.370
they're completely set that they are not going to come back to Islam?

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:44.400
They will not consider what the Prophet is saying.

00:02:44.570 --> 00:02:45.850
Is it set for them?

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:48.880
Is it set for them?
أَمْ أَبْرَمُوٓاْ أَمْرًا

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:52.360
So now we're comparing two things.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:54.860
The Ayah is not talking about construction.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:58.350
The Ayah is not talking about tying beams. It's not about a rope.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:00.060
It's actually about the decision.

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:03.760
Sometimes you make a decision, but you're not sure, you might go back on it.

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:06.450
You might listen to reason. You might appeal.

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:09.060
But then sometimes you make a decision

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:10.460
and it's done.

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:13.820
So Allah is asking a very powerful question of the Quraysh.

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:18.280
Have they made up their mind that no matter what the Prophet says ﷺ ,

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:21.680
no matter what Ayah gets revealed, they will not listen.

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:26.350
Is that the case? Allah is not saying that is the case. He's asking the question:

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:27.460
Is that the case?

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:34.590
And so He says, Allah says, if that is the case
فَإِنَّا مُبْرِمُونَ

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:37.560
Then We have tied the rope also.

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:40.250
If they've tied their rope,

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:43.480
then We've tied Our rope. So now there's two ropes.

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:46.520
There is their rope and there's Allah's rope.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:50.290
There's them tying a knot, and there's Allah tying a knot. When they tied a knot

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:54.060
I told you that is because they are stubborn and they want to stay on Shirk.

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:55.280
They don't want to accept Islam.

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:56.950
They don't want to accept the Oneness of Allah,

00:03:56.950 --> 00:03:59.401
the message of the Prophet ﷺ

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:05.711
But when Allah ties his rope, what He's saying is fine, I will make you permanent that way.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:08.620
You want to stay like that?

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:12.260
Then I will make sure that I put a rope on top of your rope and it's done.

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:13.690
It's sealed, it's settled.

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:17.550
You know how Allah says in different places in Qur'an Allah says, He's sealed their hearts.

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:21.160
Which means they will not come back, it's sealed, it's locked.

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:23.160
There's no change possible anymore.

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:27.090
Now that same lock is being described as the rope is tied.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:30.380
But what's really remarkable here in this beautiful Ayah is

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:32.760
not just a comparison between the tying of a rope

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:34.710
and the two kinds of ropes.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:34.870
You know,

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:37.100
Allah's decision and their decision and the

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:39.790
finality and the permanence of these decisions.

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:41.060
There's something even more beautiful

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:45.560
happening and scary happening here that actually has a huge lesson for Muslims

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:48.850
and and and the way we understand our faith.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:52.150
When they tied their rope,

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:53.460
أَمْ أَبْرَمُوٓاْ أَمْرًا

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:56.060
it was actually a verb.

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:57.760
It's a verb,

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:00.560
Abramu (ابرمُ) it's a past tense verb.

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:04.300
When Allah ties His rope it's actually a noun

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:07.260
فَإِنَّا مُبْرِمُونَ  It's an Ism Fa'il (اسم فاعل) for those of you that are familiar.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:10.770
It's a noun. Now I know you don't remember

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:13.080
anything from last night because it was really hot.

00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:17.410
But verbs are? Help me out. Verbs are

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:19.750
temporary. And nouns are

00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:20.790
permanent.

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:25.300
Interestingly enough, they have made up their mind, but rhetorically Allah is

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:29.350
saying perhaps even though they've made it up, there's something temporary in it,

00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:31.830
and Allah has made up His mind.

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:35.060
And yet when Allah makes up His decision, it is somehow what?

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:36.560
Permanent.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:40.080
Now, how does that play out? How do we understand this?

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:43.150
We understand this in the sense that in this life

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:44.850
these people have made up their mind.

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:47.650
And if they've made up their mind, fine.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.300
Allah will seal their heart.

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:52.620
Meaning Allah never seals anybody's heart until they have made up their mind.

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:56.180
Allah doesn't just randomly seal people's hearts.

00:05:56.940 --> 00:06:00.470
You don't get to say, Well Allah decided that this person will be misguided. No, no, no.

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:02.490
They had to make that decision first,

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:04.900
and they didn't just make that decision casually.

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:09.370
They were absolutely firm in that decision, tried and tested.

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:12.830
And Allah knows better than anybody else who's committed in their decision,

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:15.560
and then Allah decides to seal their heart and tie the rope.

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:20.440
But even that guy who made that decision, Judgment Day comes,

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:23.860
he sees the reality of what he was denying.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:26.050
And does he want to go back on his decision?

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:32.770
Yep. (رُّبَمَا يَوَدُّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ لَوْ كَانُواْ مُسْلِمِينَ)
Perhaps a day will come

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:35.760
disbelievers will wish that they had been Muslims.

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:39.240
They will wish that they can go back on their-- so they

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:41.690
go back to the rope and they're trying to untie it.

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:45.460
And then Allah responds, actually my rope is permanently tied.

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:47.750
It's in the noun form.

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:50.150
It's permanent. You can't go back on it,

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:51.540
you understand?

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:54.660
So the two sides of this equation are very beautiful.

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:59.370
On the one hand, Allah is even alluding to the fact that as firm as you think you are,

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:00.580
you're not that firm.

00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:02.660
When the time comes, you're going to be going back on it.

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:07.050
The next expression I want to share with you is heavy.

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:09.160
It is heavy.

00:07:10.040 --> 00:07:12.550
أَلَمْ تَرَ أَنَّهُمْ فِى كُلِّ وَادٍۢ يَهِيمُونَ

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:14.430
I'm moving along quickly now to the next one.

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:17.120
If you can show it to everybody just so they know where they are.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:22.160
أَلَمْ تَرَ أَنَّهُمْ فِى كُلِّ وَادٍۢ يَهِيمُونَ
This is an expression in the Qur'an describing poets.

00:07:23.740 --> 00:07:28.645
And to first, let me give you an easy translation of
أَلَمْ تَرَ أَنَّهُمْ فِى كُلِّ وَادٍۢ يَهِيمُونَ

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:32.670
Describing the poets Allah says, Don't you know? Didn't you see

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:34.660
that they venture off?

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:37.350
They wander off into every valley,

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:38.909
they

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:40.960
wander off into every valley.

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:44.140
Couple of things I want to share with you about

00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:46.960
the word Hama(هام) Yahimu(يهيم). Hama(هام) Yahimu(يهيم) is used for a camel

00:07:47.640 --> 00:07:49.150
when it's looking for water

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:52.460
and it's dying of thirst and it's just wandering aimlessly

00:07:52.940 --> 00:07:54.950
in any direction. That's Hama(هام) Yahimu(يهيم).

00:07:56.140 --> 00:07:59.000
Al-Hiyam (الهيام) is also used for

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:01.560
love that can get you killed.

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:02.550
Uh huh.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:05.260
Al-Hiyam (الهيام) is deadly love.

00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:11.690
The Arabs have they have 10 degrees of love in their language. There are 10 degrees of love.

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:13.350
The 10th one is Al-Hiyam (الهيام).

00:08:13.940 --> 00:08:14.960
This is the 10th one.

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:16.990
And this is the love that gets you killed.

00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:19.050
You know, somebody commits suicide because of love?

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:20.160
That would be Al-Hiyam (الهيام).

00:08:20.740 --> 00:08:23.560
Somebody takes an overdose because of love. That's Al-Hiyam (الهيام).

00:08:24.740 --> 00:08:28.010
You know, somebody's killing themselves with depression over love.

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:28.850
That's Al-Hiyam (الهيام).

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:34.740
Somebody--Al-Hiyam (الهيام) could be some mother who's killing herself with stress

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:35.860
over her son.

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:38.490
It could be some guy who loves this girl

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:40.549
but she doesn't like him and he's killing himself.

00:08:40.559 --> 00:08:41.350
That's Al-Hiyam (الهيام).

00:08:41.740 --> 00:08:47.840
It's deadly. So the 10th form of love is actually unhealthy. You don't want that.

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:48.960
It's kind of a disease.

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:50.860
It will kill you.

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:54.050
The one below that, the 9th one,

00:08:54.740 --> 00:08:56.860
which is the highest you can go if you don't want to die.

00:08:58.140 --> 00:08:59.460
Okay, the highest you can go is called

00:08:59.570 --> 00:09:00.260
Walah (وله)

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:02.160
و ل ه
Al-walah (الوله)

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:04.160
and Al-walah (الوله)

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:09.670
is actually also argued to be the same as
ء ل ه

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:11.860
from which we get
لا إله إلا الله

00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:15.660
So Al-walah (الوله) and Ilah (اله) are related to each other,

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:19.960
meaning one of the one of the meanings of Ilah (اله) is actually the object of love

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:23.650
and any any more love than that and you would what?

00:09:24.740 --> 00:09:25.360
You'd die.

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:29.220
and Walah (وله) is a kind of love, even though that's not the subject right now.

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:32.950
But, Walah (وله) is a kind of love that when you have it you don't feel pain anymore.

00:09:33.740 --> 00:09:35.280
Meaning you're really hungry.

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:38.600
But because of your love of something your love

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:40.880
of waiting for you know you're waiting for,

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:43.120
you know, I'll give you the example of the mother at the airport

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:45.400
again. The mother is waiting for her son to arrive.

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:47.960
She hasn't had lunch, but she doesn't feel hungry

00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:49.760
because the son is coming.

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:53.970
So that love that fills you even though you have a need, it's not felt anymore.

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:54.760
That's Walah (وله).

00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:57.627
And that's when we say
لا إله إلا الله

00:09:57.657 --> 00:10:01.360
our Iman in Allah and our 'Ibada to Allah is supposed to be filled with

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:05.160
so much love that we don't feel we don't feel like we're missing anything in life.

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:08.640
We're just not missing it. That's one of the meanings of Ilah.

00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:12.460
Anyway, that's on a side note. Coming back to you Yahimun (يهيمون) So it's a killer love

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:14.000
A love that will kill you,

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:17.150
drive you to insanity where you will be compared to

00:10:17.150 --> 00:10:20.160
a wandering camel that's looking for water and he is about to die.

00:10:20.740 --> 00:10:23.560
Okay? Now Allah gives this description for

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:24.950
poets.

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:28.050
وَالشُّعَرَاءُ يَتَّبِعُهُمُ الْغَاوُونَ

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:30.600
أَلَمْ تَرَ أَنَّهُمْ فِي كُلِّ وَادٍ يَهِيمُونَ

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:33.820
Didn't you know that they venture off into every valley?

00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:34.710
Now the thing is

00:10:35.140 --> 00:10:37.110
going into it, why even mention a valley?

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:39.703
The Arabs had this figure of speech. 

00:10:39.723 --> 00:10:41.060
هام في كل واد

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:46.210
He ventures off, meaning this guy goes everywhere aimlessly, pointlessly.

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:49.250
And he doesn't even know what kind of danger he's putting himself into.

00:10:49.260 --> 00:10:51.230
I want you to visualize the image here.

00:10:51.240 --> 00:10:53.540
There's a valley which means to enter the valley

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:55.450
do you travel upwards or downwards?

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:57.340
You have to travel

00:10:57.500 --> 00:11:00.450
downwards. You're up high on the mountain, you're traveling downwards,

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:04.960
which means your original position was up and your final position will be

00:11:05.340 --> 00:11:09.220
down. And up, being up is associated with being honored.

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:10.200
Having dignity,

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:15.260
having respect. And putting-- coming down is associated with humiliation.

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:17.880
So now the poet is being described as

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:20.150
someone who is willing to humiliate themselves.

00:11:20.540 --> 00:11:21.410
I'll come back to that.

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:25.250
But the first imagery is that of someone ready to put themselves down.

00:11:26.210 --> 00:11:28.750
Now the other thing is, when you go down into a valley,

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:31.150
there may be a way down,

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:33.060
but there may not be away

00:11:33.940 --> 00:11:35.460
up. Isn't that true?

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:38.060
You could get down. Gravity will help you.

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:42.410
But when you're trying to get back out, you might be stuck,

00:11:43.440 --> 00:11:46.050
and you're not even considering what kind of valley it is.

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:49.570
( كُلِّ وَادٍ) is Nakira (نكرة) suggesting, I don't even know what kind of valley this is?

00:11:49.580 --> 00:11:52.670
I don't know if there are snakes down there, dangers down there.

00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:56.500
I don't know if I'll ever be able to be able to get out. I don't know. I don't care.

00:11:56.500 --> 00:11:57.260
I'm going anyway.

00:11:58.140 --> 00:11:59.060
I'm going anyway.

00:11:59.540 --> 00:12:00.480
So what is

00:12:00.310 --> 00:12:05.030
It's not like Allah is saying or the Arabs are saying, specifically here Allah is

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:07.550
