00:25:41.940 --> 00:25:43.050
What do you imagine happened?

00:25:43.440 --> 00:25:44.530
That Allah took the town

00:25:44.690 --> 00:25:46.050
and like a Pronto Plaster

00:25:49.330 --> 00:25:51.060
Like up, flip, down.

00:25:51.940 --> 00:25:53.950
Right? That's what happened. Actually, that's not what happened.

00:25:54.840 --> 00:25:55.770
That's not what happened.

00:25:56.340 --> 00:26:00.310
I want to describe to you this is actually an example of brevity in the Qur'an.

00:26:00.310 --> 00:26:04.070
Brevity means Allah speaks very briefly and He says a lot.

00:26:04.080 --> 00:26:05.670
He just gives you an entire picture.

00:26:06.140 --> 00:26:07.670
So I want to describe what that means.

00:26:08.540 --> 00:26:10.750
First, I want to give you two meanings of the word 'Arsh (عرش).

00:26:11.140 --> 00:26:12.600
Two meanings of the word 'Arsh.

00:26:12.830 --> 00:26:14.080
The plural is used in the Ayah:

00:26:14.120 --> 00:26:16.650
وَهِيَ خَاوِيَةٌ عَلَى عُرُوشِهَا

00:26:17.040 --> 00:26:22.594
'Arsh is used for the ceiling or the roof of a building.

00:26:22.664 --> 00:26:25.710
'Arsh also used interestingly for the trellis.

00:26:25.710 --> 00:26:27.770
Let me tell you what the trellis is, I didn't know either.

00:26:28.240 --> 00:26:30.850
You know, there are some plants that are weak.

00:26:31.340 --> 00:26:34.650
They cannot stand on their own. So you put a stick in the ground

00:26:34.870 --> 00:26:36.460
and then it wraps itself around it.

00:26:37.540 --> 00:26:38.560
You know what I'm talking about?

00:26:39.040 --> 00:26:40.660
Like grape vines and things like that.

00:26:41.140 --> 00:26:43.480
That stick is called 'Arsh.

00:26:44.540 --> 00:26:47.370
The stick itself that you put in the ground is called 'Arsh.

00:26:47.480 --> 00:26:49.760
So 'Arsh has two meanings right now, one is the

00:26:50.240 --> 00:26:52.990
roof, the ceiling and the second meaning is

00:26:53.640 --> 00:26:54.550
the stick in the ground.

00:26:54.800 --> 00:26:55.170
Now

00:26:55.940 --> 00:26:57.350
let me start with the stick in the ground.

00:26:58.040 --> 00:26:59.860
In the story of the two gardeners

00:27:00.640 --> 00:27:07.170
Surat al-Kahf, two gardeners. The gardener's farm was surrounded by palm trees.

00:27:08.240 --> 00:27:11.190
His farm was surrounded by palm trees so that if it's windy,

00:27:11.200 --> 00:27:13.670
what protects the delicate plants in the middle?

00:27:14.410 --> 00:27:15.270
The palm trees.

00:27:16.340 --> 00:27:19.460
So he put palm trees not only because or date palms even,

00:27:19.460 --> 00:27:23.450
not only because it will give him fruits, but it was also his security system.

00:27:24.240 --> 00:27:24.770
Okay?

00:27:25.340 --> 00:27:27.780
And in the middle he used to have 'Anab (اعناب)

00:27:27.750 --> 00:27:30.480
Nakhil (نخيل) like you know, delicate plants,

00:27:31.040 --> 00:27:32.270
delicate plants in the middle.

00:27:33.840 --> 00:27:37.860
Now the thing is, when Allah decided to destroy his garden,

00:27:38.740 --> 00:27:41.420
Allah described the description with one phrase:

00:27:41.544 --> 00:27:44.154
وَهِيَ خَاوِيَةٌ عَلَى عُرُوشِهَا

00:27:44.220 --> 00:27:47.670
The town was turned over on top of its

00:27:48.140 --> 00:27:49.060
trellises.

00:27:49.440 --> 00:27:50.260
In other words,

00:27:50.550 --> 00:27:52.670
those sticks in the middle of the farm

00:27:53.240 --> 00:27:56.650
Allah made the winds come and the destruction come that those trees that

00:27:56.650 --> 00:28:00.820
were there to protect the garden fell on top of the delicate plants.

00:28:00.830 --> 00:28:05.060
So not only did the trees get destroyed, the delicate plants got destroyed.

00:28:05.740 --> 00:28:08.600
That's the description being given of that garden being destroyed.

00:28:08.610 --> 00:28:10.990
See, the guy thought this will protect it.

00:28:11.000 --> 00:28:14.050
And Allah took his security system and made it the attack.

00:28:14.840 --> 00:28:16.360
He reversed it. Subhanallah.

00:28:16.940 --> 00:28:18.600
Now what about the

00:28:18.600 --> 00:28:21.810
the nations that are destroyed and Allah says they were turned over on their roofs?

00:28:22.410 --> 00:28:25.060
The other meaning of 'Arsh is roof right?

00:28:25.440 --> 00:28:28.630
And the towns were turned over on their roof. Let me tell you what that's describing.

00:28:28.630 --> 00:28:29.360
It's amazing.

00:28:30.050 --> 00:28:32.560
Sometimes Allah destroys a nation by an earthquake.

00:28:33.340 --> 00:28:37.560
Sometimes the nation is destroyed by fire from the sky. A meteor shower.

00:28:38.340 --> 00:28:39.660
Sometimes it's a flood.

00:28:40.140 --> 00:28:42.170
Sometimes it's a tornado or a wind,

00:28:42.840 --> 00:28:44.730
right? Different kinds of destruction.

00:28:44.900 --> 00:28:47.720
Now let's imagine one of those happened. Everybody's dead.

00:28:47.970 --> 00:28:51.170
And the whole town the buildings are standing, but they're damaged, right?

00:28:51.640 --> 00:28:55.770
The buildings are there, but they are damaged and there are people left or no?

00:28:56.840 --> 00:28:58.010
They're not left.

00:28:58.020 --> 00:29:00.620
By the way, when a building is-- when buildings get damaged,

00:29:00.620 --> 00:29:03.950
the first thing that gets damaged is the roof; it's the most exposed part.

00:29:04.940 --> 00:29:07.670
It's the one that least work is put into.

00:29:07.670 --> 00:29:11.200
It's the weakest part. Foundation you put in the most work; roof

00:29:11.200 --> 00:29:13.670
you put in the least work because you can't put too heavy of

00:29:13.670 --> 00:29:16.370
a roof because it's too much pressure on the rest of the building.

00:29:16.370 --> 00:29:17.270
So you make it light.

00:29:18.140 --> 00:29:21.860
So the roof gets damaged. That's why your roof starts leaking if it rains too much

00:29:22.540 --> 00:29:26.510
or you get issues in your roof and pieces of it fly off and things like that. Right?

00:29:26.800 --> 00:29:28.960
Now, nobody's maintaining these buildings.

00:29:29.540 --> 00:29:31.180
Nobody's maintaining these buildings,

00:29:31.190 --> 00:29:34.120
which means that the roof gets weaker and weaker

00:29:34.120 --> 00:29:36.260
and weaker and eventually what happens to the roof?

00:29:36.740 --> 00:29:39.480
Imagine, 100 years went by. Nobody's lived in this village.

00:29:39.490 --> 00:29:41.270
What happens to those roofs?

00:29:42.540 --> 00:29:43.670
They fall.

00:29:44.230 --> 00:29:46.860
Now you've got four walls and in the middle what's there?

00:29:48.340 --> 00:29:49.860
The roof is sitting on the floor now.

00:29:50.240 --> 00:29:51.100
It caved in.

00:29:51.860 --> 00:29:56.270
And these when you go to these old abandoned places, you just see walls, right?

00:29:56.640 --> 00:29:57.960
Broken down walls,

00:29:58.740 --> 00:29:59.790
and they're just standing there.

00:29:59.790 --> 00:30:03.030
Now one of the things that holds the walls together is the pressure from the roof,

00:30:03.040 --> 00:30:03.940
but no longer

00:30:03.960 --> 00:30:09.860
there's no longer a roof, so these walls get exposed to moisture and mold and rust

00:30:10.440 --> 00:30:12.220
and insects and all of it.

00:30:12.580 --> 00:30:16.050
Then eventually winds come and what happens to these walls?

00:30:16.740 --> 00:30:18.960
They fall on top of the already fallen

00:30:19.740 --> 00:30:20.550
roof.

00:30:20.830 --> 00:30:23.360
Does this happen overnight, or does it take centuries?

00:30:24.740 --> 00:30:27.250
It takes decades and centuries to do this.

00:30:27.740 --> 00:30:31.600
Allah is not just telling us that the town was flipped over on the roof,

00:30:31.610 --> 00:30:36.630
Allah is saying Allah destroyed the town in such a way that generations went by to the

00:30:36.630 --> 00:30:39.340
point where even whatever walls were left fell

00:30:39.340 --> 00:30:41.450
on top of the already collapsed roofs.

00:30:42.340 --> 00:30:46.660
So line this one small phrase isn't just talking about the extent

00:30:47.040 --> 00:30:48.230
of destruction.

00:30:48.240 --> 00:30:50.620
Allah is also talking about the span.

00:30:50.630 --> 00:30:54.860
How long the time went by and nobody could live in these places.

00:30:55.740 --> 00:30:58.420
It's captured in just one phrase
وَهِيَ خَاوِيَةٌ عَلَى عُرُوشِهَا

00:30:59.040 --> 00:31:03.650
So this was our first exploration; our first exploration was how does Allah

00:31:03.650 --> 00:31:05.060
use small phrases

00:31:05.840 --> 00:31:08.410
that Arabs used to use back in the day and say amazing

00:31:08.410 --> 00:31:11.580
things in the Qur'an and there are literally thousands of them.

00:31:11.590 --> 00:31:14.270
But I wanted to give you a sampling. That was section one.

