And he used to be

00:31:52.340 --> 00:31:53.450
pretty much a non-Muslim.

00:31:54.840 --> 00:31:56.700
He was raised in Iraq.

00:31:56.710 --> 00:32:01.770
He was part of the Communist Party, the Baathist Party, at one point back in the day.

00:32:02.840 --> 00:32:07.040
And when he was there, he loved language.

00:32:07.040 --> 00:32:10.760
So he studied linguistics and Arabic and, you know, Arab nationalism.

00:32:11.440 --> 00:32:14.860
So he studied Arabic under the banner of Arab nationalism, not because of Islam.

00:32:15.740 --> 00:32:20.170
And one of his interest was that he actually did not want to study the Qur'an.

00:32:21.240 --> 00:32:23.850
He wanted to study Arabic, but he did not want to study

00:32:24.240 --> 00:32:24.960
the Qur'an.

00:32:25.440 --> 00:32:27.170
He refused to study it. It is beneath him.

00:32:28.440 --> 00:32:30.650
Somebody eventually and he used to by the way,

00:32:30.660 --> 00:32:33.190
you know he was in charge of developing

00:32:33.190 --> 00:32:35.390
the Arabic curriculum for high schools in Baghdad.

00:32:35.400 --> 00:32:38.220
He was in charge of like the PhD program in Arabic

00:32:38.220 --> 00:32:42.180
studies and literature at the University of Baghdad, he was I mean high up.

