One of his PhD students challenged him and said,

00:32:44.940 --> 00:32:47.960
Why don't you write a criticism of the Qur'an if you think you're above it?

00:32:49.040 --> 00:32:51.460
Why don't you write a linguistic criticism?

00:32:51.940 --> 00:32:53.770
So he did. He decided to write one,

00:32:54.840 --> 00:32:58.410
and when he did, he wrote a book called the title of the book

00:32:58.430 --> 00:33:03.186
(نبوة محمد من الشك الى اليقين) The Prophethood of Mohammed ﷺ

00:33:03.180 --> 00:33:05.850
My journey from doubt to conviction.

00:33:06.830 --> 00:33:10.760
In his process of writing the criticism against the Qur'an, he became a believer.

00:33:12.040 --> 00:33:14.800
I just recently got a copy of the book and I read through it,

00:33:14.810 --> 00:33:16.760
even though I've been reading his books for some time.

00:33:16.770 --> 00:33:17.460
And it is--

00:33:18.240 --> 00:33:19.150
It's a book

00:33:19.390 --> 00:33:20.460
That's a must read.

00:33:20.940 --> 00:33:23.550
Inshallah hopefully one of my students will translate it

00:33:24.240 --> 00:33:24.950
باذنه تعالى

00:33:24.950 --> 00:33:27.380
It's fascinating stuff from beginning to end, especially,

00:33:27.380 --> 00:33:29.160
his introduction is awesome.

00:33:29.540 --> 00:33:30.350
It's awesome.

00:33:31.040 --> 00:33:34.160
But anyway, so he now he became a fan of the Qur'an,

00:33:34.640 --> 00:33:38.860
and he's been studying language and he's mastered language for decades already

00:33:38.870 --> 00:33:41.670
Arabic. But never applied it to the Qur'an.

00:33:42.140 --> 00:33:47.030
So he I like to say he brought a fresh set of eyes to the Qur'an. Why?

00:33:47.040 --> 00:33:50.560
Because when people study Arabic, they study Arabic and Qur'an hand in hand.

00:33:51.140 --> 00:33:52.670
They study them together all the time.

00:33:53.440 --> 00:33:56.050
And when people get in depth studies in Arabic,

00:33:56.050 --> 00:33:58.450
they usually do it because they're getting in depth studies in

00:33:58.840 --> 00:33:59.440
the Qur'an.

00:33:59.440 --> 00:34:02.520
But this man studied Arabic in depth not to access the Qur'an,

00:34:02.520 --> 00:34:03.670
but for Arabic itself.

00:34:04.040 --> 00:34:06.640
And eventually he applied what he learned to the Qur'an.

00:34:06.650 --> 00:34:09.870
So it was like he's looking at it from a different angle than everybody else.

00:34:10.540 --> 00:34:12.159
This has got a different perspective,

00:34:12.940 --> 00:34:15.060
and boy is that a different perspective.

00:34:15.940 --> 00:34:19.420
He started writing book after book after book after book

00:34:19.429 --> 00:34:22.060
on what makes the Qur'an unique in its expression.

