00:35:22.440 --> 00:35:23.250
So

00:35:23.640 --> 00:35:24.360
let's begin.

00:35:26.440 --> 00:35:31.360
How come the Qur'an uses--what's the word for the City of the Prophet?

00:35:31.740 --> 00:35:32.250
Anyone know?

00:35:33.340 --> 00:35:33.970
Medina

00:35:35.540 --> 00:35:36.970
Medinat-un-Nabi  really

00:35:37.440 --> 00:35:39.170
Medinat-un-Nabi or al-Medina.

00:35:40.040 --> 00:35:41.170
What's the other name of it?

00:35:42.440 --> 00:35:43.060
Yathrib.

00:35:44.020 --> 00:35:46.970
Six times in the Qur'an Allah uses al-Medina

00:35:48.140 --> 00:35:50.060
only once in the Qur'an He uses Yathrib.

00:35:52.140 --> 00:35:54.260
So why does He use Medina? And why does He use

00:35:54.740 --> 00:35:55.360
Yathrib?

00:35:56.340 --> 00:35:59.040
And if these are both referring to the same city,

00:35:59.050 --> 00:36:01.590
then actually you should be able to use either one.

00:36:01.600 --> 00:36:02.460
No problem.

00:36:03.130 --> 00:36:06.400
You understand? So how come the Qur'an uses one as opposed to the other.

00:36:06.400 --> 00:36:07.350
That's the question here.

00:36:08.710 --> 00:36:11.540
The thing is, Medina is not the original name of the city.

00:36:12.530 --> 00:36:14.870
Medina is the given name of the city.

00:36:14.880 --> 00:36:19.550
It was only called Medina because it's short for Medinat-un-Nabi, the city of the

00:36:20.030 --> 00:36:20.590
Prophet ﷺ.

00:36:21.890 --> 00:36:24.360
Which means it was only called Medina after the Prophet

00:36:24.360 --> 00:36:27.550
moved there and became the de facto governor of Medina.

00:36:28.330 --> 00:36:30.040
Once he became the governor of Medina

00:36:30.050 --> 00:36:34.240
then it was called Medinat-un-Nabi. Before he moved there what was its name?

00:36:35.330 --> 00:36:35.700
Yathrib.

00:36:36.330 --> 00:36:36.680
Yathrib.

00:36:38.430 --> 00:36:41.530
So it's interesting that every time we talk about Medina,

00:36:41.540 --> 00:36:44.260
we find-- we talk about the city.

00:36:44.260 --> 00:36:46.050
We usually find Medina in the Qur'an.

00:36:46.430 --> 00:36:49.430
It is as though Allah Himself wants us to know that it's no longer Yathrib

00:36:49.590 --> 00:36:50.540
it is actually

00:36:50.930 --> 00:36:52.460
Medina. It's the Prophet's city now.

00:36:52.930 --> 00:36:53.930
It's his city now.

00:36:53.940 --> 00:36:56.830
Every time we use the word Medina for Medina, we don't call it Yathrib anymore.

00:36:56.830 --> 00:36:59.390
Nobody says I'm going to Yathrib after Makkah after 'Umrah

00:36:59.390 --> 00:37:00.740
then I'm gonna go to Yathrib for a little bit.

00:37:00.750 --> 00:37:03.160
Nobody says that anymore. They say I'm going to go where?

00:37:03.700 --> 00:37:06.350
To Medina. Because Allah wanted it to be named this way.

00:37:07.130 --> 00:37:09.690
But I want you to know something. Let's go back in time. Let's go

00:37:09.690 --> 00:37:10.700
at the time of the Prophet ﷺ.

00:37:12.170 --> 00:37:15.360
In Medina, you had a group of people called the hypocrites.

00:37:16.300 --> 00:37:17.150
Yes.

00:37:18.130 --> 00:37:20.650
And interestingly enough, the Munafiqun

00:37:21.430 --> 00:37:24.175
they were not loyal to the Prophet ﷺ

00:37:25.330 --> 00:37:28.510
Which means they did not like the fact that this

00:37:28.510 --> 00:37:31.150
city that used to be Yathrib has now become

00:37:31.930 --> 00:37:32.550
Medina.

00:37:33.630 --> 00:37:37.250
So the one group of people who did not like the word Medina is who?

00:37:38.310 --> 00:37:39.040
The Munafiqun

00:37:39.380 --> 00:37:40.150
they didn't like it.

00:37:41.430 --> 00:37:44.910
But the problem is they don't come out in the open and say we don't like it.

00:37:44.920 --> 00:37:45.960
We want it to be Yathrib.

00:37:47.330 --> 00:37:49.160
They still use what word?

00:37:49.530 --> 00:37:51.710
Medina. Now, why do you think the Munafiq

00:37:51.740 --> 00:37:54.460
the hypocrite who does not like the word Medina?

00:37:54.470 --> 00:37:57.250
Because it describes the fact that the governorship of

00:37:57.250 --> 00:37:59.430
Medina is in the hands of the Prophet ﷺ.

00:38:00.390 --> 00:38:04.440
He doesn't like that fact, but he still uses Medina. Why does he use it?

00:38:04.920 --> 00:38:05.750
That's the question.

00:38:06.620 --> 00:38:08.560
He uses Medina to at least

00:38:08.790 --> 00:38:09.650
pretend

00:38:10.320 --> 00:38:11.340
that he is loyal.

00:38:12.220 --> 00:38:12.940
You understand?

00:38:14.620 --> 00:38:17.700
He has to show at least to the Prophet ﷺ that he's still

00:38:17.940 --> 00:38:20.340
loyal. So in Surat al-Munafiqun

00:38:20.720 --> 00:38:22.050
the Surah of the hypocrites,

00:38:22.480 --> 00:38:25.360
they want to impress the Prophet ﷺ.

00:38:25.340 --> 00:38:28.049
اتَّخَذُوا أَيْمَانَهُمْ جُنَّةً

00:38:28.420 --> 00:38:29.940
So you know

00:38:29.899 --> 00:38:32.389
لَئِن رَّجَعْنَا إِلَى الْمَدِينَةِ

00:38:33.620 --> 00:38:36.070
They use the word, the hypocrites use the word Medina. Why?

00:38:36.070 --> 00:38:37.420
Because they want to tell the Prophet ﷺ

00:38:37.570 --> 00:38:41.150
No, no, no, you're you're our leader. Sure, you're our leader. We want to obey you.

00:38:42.620 --> 00:38:46.200
Now here's the amazing lesson of that Allah teaches us by using Medina

00:38:46.200 --> 00:38:48.910
and Yathrib. It's not just interesting usage. There are lessons in it.

00:38:48.960 --> 00:38:50.150
So here's one lesson

00:38:51.530 --> 00:38:54.580
the hypocrite stays hidden among the Muslims.

00:38:55.320 --> 00:38:57.540
Yes, they're very good at hiding among the Muslims,

00:38:58.120 --> 00:39:01.750
but they can only hide successfully when times are easy.

00:39:03.320 --> 00:39:06.340
And the hypocrite cannot hide easily when times are

00:39:07.320 --> 00:39:07.950
difficult.

00:39:08.730 --> 00:39:12.540
I'll say that again, hypocrites can blend in easily when times are what?

00:39:13.120 --> 00:39:16.410
Easy. And they don't-- are not able to hide themselves

00:39:16.410 --> 00:39:19.030
when times are difficult, they become exposed.

00:39:20.720 --> 00:39:25.560
When they moved to Medina, no battles have happened yet times are still

00:39:25.670 --> 00:39:26.240
easy.

00:39:27.820 --> 00:39:30.040
When times are easy, they call the city what?

00:39:30.920 --> 00:39:31.450
Medina.

00:39:32.520 --> 00:39:34.250
Then let's turn to Surat al-Ahzab.

00:39:35.120 --> 00:39:37.340
Surat al-Ahzab the city of Medina was

00:39:37.340 --> 00:39:40.200
surrounded by virtually every tribe of Arabia.

00:39:40.210 --> 00:39:44.630
The Makkans made an alliance with a bunch of different tribes, Let's attack the city.

00:39:44.640 --> 00:39:47.830
Let's surround it. And once we get in, we will commit genocide.

00:39:47.830 --> 00:39:48.950
We will leave no one alive.

00:39:49.720 --> 00:39:51.230
We'll get rid of everyone.

00:39:51.410 --> 00:39:56.040
And the only thing protecting the city from being torn apart is the trench.

00:39:56.720 --> 00:39:59.200
Called the Battle of the Trench, al-Khunduq. You guys know this.

00:40:00.510 --> 00:40:06.250
In this situation the hypocrites of Medina they're inside the city thinking, Well

00:40:06.250 --> 00:40:09.510
we only went along and we only showed our loyalty because we thought

00:40:09.510 --> 00:40:12.690
the Muslims are gonna win a lot of battles and we'll get rich.

00:40:12.700 --> 00:40:14.270
But that doesn't look like it's going to happen.

00:40:14.270 --> 00:40:15.740
It looks like we're all going to get killed.

00:40:16.510 --> 00:40:18.940
This whole Medina business was not a good deal.

00:40:19.910 --> 00:40:21.104
So they say, وقالو

00:40:21.216 --> 00:40:26.244
يَا أَهْلَ يَثْرِبَ لا مُقَامَ لَكُمْ  فَارْجِعُوا

00:40:26.410 --> 00:40:30.000
They said, Hey, people of Yathrib, you've got no place to go.

00:40:30.000 --> 00:40:34.930
Let's go back to the way things were. Come on, let's go back and make it what, again?

00:40:35.510 --> 00:40:36.740
Yathrib again.

00:40:37.410 --> 00:40:40.950
Now, just because of the fact that they used the word Yathrib

00:40:40.960 --> 00:40:44.820
didn't they prove that they're not loyal to the Prophet ﷺ?

00:40:45.610 --> 00:40:46.994
So, Allah 'azzawajal

00:40:47.020 --> 00:40:50.230
exposes the hypocrites from their own mouth

00:40:50.610 --> 00:40:51.930
when times are difficult.

00:40:53.410 --> 00:40:58.330
And they will, from their own mouth, talk a lot about loyalty when times are

00:40:59.210 --> 00:40:59.740
easy.

00:41:00.610 --> 00:41:03.500
You don't have to accuse the hypocrite of being a hypocrite.

00:41:03.510 --> 00:41:04.710
They'll tell you themselves.

00:41:05.610 --> 00:41:08.330
Just wait for difficult times, that's all.

00:41:09.110 --> 00:41:10.780
That's what Allah 'azzawajal does in the Qur'an

00:41:10.800 --> 00:41:13.130
So why why Yathrib and why Medina.

00:41:13.610 --> 00:41:15.320
I'll give you one more and there's your break.

00:41:16.020 --> 00:41:18.940
It's actually pretty simple and straightforward. I'll even skip that one.

00:41:19.610 --> 00:41:21.612
I'll give you
بَلْ عَجِبُوٓاْ أَن جَآءَهُم مُّنذِرٌ مِّنْهُمْ

00:41:21.650 --> 00:41:23.930
I love this one. And can you show it on the screen, please.

00:41:24.710 --> 00:41:25.820
I want to show you guys something.

00:41:27.010 --> 00:41:27.966
Two Ayat in the Qur'an

00:41:27.940 --> 00:41:30.606
I'm comparing here,
بَلْ عَجِبُوٓاْ

00:41:30.630 --> 00:41:33.810
Keep showing it keep showing it. Oh, yeah, one of them.

00:41:33.810 --> 00:41:38.100
Okay, so (بَلْ عَجِبُوٓاْ) and (وَعَجِبُوٓاْ). (بَلْ عَجِبُوٓاْ) Rather, they found it

00:41:38.100 --> 00:41:40.597
strange. The Ayah underneath it (وَعَجِبُوٓاْ)

00:41:40.130 --> 00:41:41.100
And they found it

00:41:41.100 --> 00:41:45.030
strange. Isn't it similar? In both cases, the discussion begins with

00:41:45.167 --> 00:41:48.030
the Mushrikun found something strange.

00:41:48.210 --> 00:41:49.817
Now what did they find strange?

00:41:49.857 --> 00:41:54.330
( أَن جَآءَهُم مُّنذِرٌ مِّنْهُمْ) That a warner came to them from among themselves.

00:41:55.210 --> 00:41:59.310
What did the Mushrikun found strange? That a warner from among themselves came.

00:41:59.320 --> 00:42:01.510
Who is this warner? Who is it talking about?

00:42:02.800 --> 00:42:03.930
Call it out. Call it out.

00:42:07.080 --> 00:42:10.320
By the way, you guys better get loud because I'll stop talking forever.

00:42:12.000 --> 00:42:15.230
When I ask you a question, call it out. Who is the warner?

00:42:16.820 --> 00:42:17.930
Rasulallah ﷺ.

00:42:18.700 --> 00:42:22.420
Now the thing is, why is that strange? Let me explain why that's strange.

00:42:23.700 --> 00:42:27.720
A warner comes with some dangerous information from the outside.

00:42:29.300 --> 00:42:31.610
There's an army coming from the other side of the mountain.

00:42:32.700 --> 00:42:34.620
You would have to go outside,

00:42:35.100 --> 00:42:39.120
see the army, come back and say, hey, there's an army.

00:42:40.100 --> 00:42:43.520
So a warner has to not be from you. He has to be from outside you.

00:42:44.800 --> 00:42:46.260
What kind of warner is this?

00:42:46.260 --> 00:42:48.440
He's sitting with us and he's telling us warnings

00:42:48.440 --> 00:42:51.440
about some world and some angels and some Jahannam

00:42:51.440 --> 00:42:52.770
and some this and some that.

00:42:52.770 --> 00:42:53.730
What is he talking about?

00:42:54.200 --> 00:42:56.430
They find it very strange that he's a warner from

00:42:56.800 --> 00:42:59.790
among themselves. You understand? Both Ayat talk about it.

00:43:00.160 --> 00:43:02.445
فَقالَ الْكافِرُونَ هذا شَيْءٌ عَجِيبٌ

00:43:02.455 --> 00:43:04.750
Disbeliever said this is a strange thing.

00:43:05.400 --> 00:43:08.400
When they talk about a warner this guy's giving us warnings ﷺ

00:43:08.600 --> 00:43:13.884
they say this is a strange thing.
هذا شَيْءٌ عَجِيبٌ

00:43:13.900 --> 00:43:15.430
Now you switch over a little bit

00:43:15.900 --> 00:43:17.010
and I want to show this to you.

00:43:20.900 --> 00:43:22.010
Oh, that's so small.

00:43:22.980 --> 00:43:23.520
Big.

00:43:24.800 --> 00:43:27.670
هذا شَيْءٌ عَجِيبٌ

00:43:31.900 --> 00:43:33.310
What does it mean (هذا شَيْءٌ عَجِيبٌ)?

00:43:34.900 --> 00:43:36.520
This is a strange thing.

00:43:37.300 --> 00:43:39.220
This is a strange thing.

00:43:39.800 --> 00:43:41.160
And the other Ayah says

00:43:41.300 --> 00:43:46.320
إِنَّ هَٰذَا لَشَيْءٌ عُجَابٌ

00:43:49.600 --> 00:43:50.890
What's the difference between the first one

00:43:50.890 --> 00:43:52.620
the second one? Do they both have (هذا) and (شيء)?

00:43:54.400 --> 00:43:54.930
But

00:43:56.600 --> 00:43:58.610
does the first--the second one has something more?

00:43:59.600 --> 00:44:00.410
What does it have?

00:44:00.510 --> 00:44:01.063
It has (إِنَّ)

00:44:01.010 --> 00:44:02.300
What else is more?

00:44:03.490 --> 00:44:06.023
The (شيء) has (لشيء)

00:44:06.790 --> 00:44:08.710
And then instead of (عجيب) what are we saying?

00:44:09.590 --> 00:44:10.220
(عجاب)

00:44:10.990 --> 00:44:12.610
So there are three differences.

00:44:13.390 --> 00:44:15.100
Can you see that? That there are three differences?

00:44:15.690 --> 00:44:17.476
One is (هَذَا شَيْءٌ عَجِيبٌ). The second one--

00:44:17.530 --> 00:44:21.466
The first difference is (اِنَّ) the second difference is (ل) and the third difference is

00:44:21.490 --> 00:44:22.810
(عجاب) you with me?

00:44:23.290 --> 00:44:24.510
Okay, now go back.

00:44:25.590 --> 00:44:28.017
وَعَجِبُوٓاْ أَن جَآءَهُم مُّنذِرٌ مِّنْهُمْ

00:44:28.010 --> 00:44:29.217
I'm reading the second Ayah.

00:44:29.210 --> 00:44:31.140
They find it strange that a warner came to them

00:44:31.140 --> 00:44:34.248
from among themselves
وَقَالَ ٱلْكَٰفِرُونَ هَٰذَا سَٰحِرٌ كَذَّابٌ

00:44:34.240 --> 00:44:37.010
And the disbeliever said, this is a magician,

00:44:37.390 --> 00:44:40.280
a liar who keeps lying over and over again.

00:44:40.360 --> 00:44:45.750
أَجَعَلَ ٱلْءَالِهَةَ إِلَٰهًا وَٰحِدًا
Did he take all of our gods and turned them into one?

00:44:45.790 --> 00:44:49.000
Did he take all of our Aliha (اله) and turn them into one?

00:44:48.990 --> 00:44:51.040
إِنَّ هَٰذَا لَشَيْءٌ عُجَابٌ

00:44:51.080 --> 00:44:53.300
You see where I got that second part from?

00:44:53.290 --> 00:44:54.010
Now, listen,

00:44:54.690 --> 00:44:57.110
let me explain these insults against the Prophet ﷺ.

00:44:57.760 --> 00:44:58.920
What did they call him?

00:45:00.490 --> 00:45:01.600
Magician and what?

00:45:02.390 --> 00:45:05.190
Liar. Now is the Prophet ﷺ

00:45:05.560 --> 00:45:06.800
doing any magic tricks?

00:45:09.090 --> 00:45:10.800
I mean, there's no rabbit out of a hat.

00:45:11.490 --> 00:45:13.410
There's no staff turning into a snake.

00:45:14.090 --> 00:45:15.590
There's no water parting.

00:45:16.690 --> 00:45:17.500
What is he doing?

00:45:18.790 --> 00:45:20.310
What is he doing? He's reciting Qur'an.

00:45:21.590 --> 00:45:23.720
Is Qur'an something you see or something you hear?

00:45:24.970 --> 00:45:27.010
Tell me when you hear something do you call it magic?

00:45:29.280 --> 00:45:31.310
Somebody says something verse you're like magical.

00:45:32.090 --> 00:45:32.600
Do you do that?

00:45:33.890 --> 00:45:36.110
No. When do you use the word magic?

00:45:37.390 --> 00:45:38.500
When you see something?

00:45:39.290 --> 00:45:42.310
It was floating in the air like

00:45:42.790 --> 00:45:45.610
Jinn I knew he was a Jinn. Like you know, like that sort of thing.

00:45:47.990 --> 00:45:52.310
You know? Magic is for something that you see.

00:45:53.290 --> 00:45:55.300
How are they calling the Qur'an

00:45:55.990 --> 00:45:56.710
magic?

00:45:57.790 --> 00:45:59.830
They're calling or they're calling the Prophet ﷺ

00:45:59.830 --> 00:46:03.910
a magician because the effect it has on people

00:46:04.980 --> 00:46:06.710
and the effect it has on them,

00:46:07.680 --> 00:46:08.790
even themselves,

00:46:09.480 --> 00:46:14.230
they cannot explain it using common sense. And when you cannot explain things

00:46:14.550 --> 00:46:15.690
through common sense,

00:46:15.800 --> 00:46:18.300
you call it a mystery of the unknown.

00:46:18.680 --> 00:46:21.150
And the mystery of the unknown is called

00:46:21.260 --> 00:46:22.060
magic.

00:46:22.310 --> 00:46:23.200
In other words,

00:46:23.350 --> 00:46:24.910
this is a kind of belief.

00:46:26.280 --> 00:46:29.020
You know, we say believers have Iman in the Ghaib (غيب), yes?

00:46:30.180 --> 00:46:34.100
When someone calls someone a magic magician, they also have iman in the Ghaib (غيب).

00:46:35.780 --> 00:46:38.420
In other words, in calling Rasulullah ﷺ

00:46:38.570 --> 00:46:40.360
a magician

00:46:40.480 --> 00:46:42.240
the Kuffar admitted.

00:46:42.780 --> 00:46:46.860
They admitted that this cannot be explained through common sense.

00:46:47.090 --> 00:46:49.200
This is above and beyond explanation.

00:46:50.380 --> 00:46:51.210
It's magic.

00:46:51.880 --> 00:46:52.410
Mhm,

00:46:53.380 --> 00:46:55.300
Meaning they already took a leap of faith.

00:46:56.380 --> 00:46:59.170
We think of him being called a magician as an insult.

00:46:59.180 --> 00:47:01.490
It's not only an insult, it is an admission

00:47:01.790 --> 00:47:02.670
of their defeat

00:47:03.450 --> 00:47:04.780
that they couldn't explain away the Qur'an.

00:47:04.940 --> 00:47:08.210
You understand this point? Very heavy. It's really important to understand

00:47:08.580 --> 00:47:10.410
why in the world would they call him a magician?

00:47:11.380 --> 00:47:14.200
But they didn't just call him a magician. What else did they call him?

00:47:15.380 --> 00:47:17.650
Kazzab (كذاب)what's even in the word Kazzab

00:47:17.650 --> 00:47:20.440
he's not a Kazib (كاذب), Kazib means he's a liar but Kazzab

00:47:20.440 --> 00:47:22.910
means someone who lies over and over and over and over again.

00:47:22.920 --> 00:47:27.100
Even that is actually not only an insult, it is also a compliment.

00:47:27.980 --> 00:47:28.790
Let me tell you how.

00:47:29.280 --> 00:47:31.790
Somebody says Astaghfirullah how can Kazzab be a compliment?

00:47:32.280 --> 00:47:34.800
How can they? How could this be a good thing? Let me tell you,

00:47:35.780 --> 00:47:37.000
be patient, I'll tell you.

00:47:39.180 --> 00:47:41.400
A liar goes to someone and tells a lie.

00:47:43.040 --> 00:47:44.500
Then his lie gets discovered

00:47:45.680 --> 00:47:49.210
when his lie gets discovered, is he able to lie to the same person again?

00:47:50.080 --> 00:47:51.490
No. He finds a new victim.

00:47:52.880 --> 00:47:55.970
Then he goes and lies to that person. His lie gets discovered.

00:47:55.970 --> 00:47:58.700
He has to move out of town and go lie somewhere else.

00:47:59.380 --> 00:48:01.020
And then he goes out away somewhere else.

00:48:01.020 --> 00:48:04.200
Because once his lies get called a lie, he gives up.

00:48:05.930 --> 00:48:08.000
The idea that someone comes to you

00:48:08.770 --> 00:48:09.900
you call him a liar

00:48:10.270 --> 00:48:12.700
you shoo him away. He comes back to you.

00:48:13.270 --> 00:48:17.870
You put him away. He comes back to you. You put him away. He doesn't go away.

00:48:17.880 --> 00:48:21.280
All other liars lie one time, they get caught and what happens?

00:48:21.770 --> 00:48:25.390
They go away. This man doesn't stop. He keeps telling me the same lies.

00:48:26.670 --> 00:48:30.200
In other words, he's not like any other liar I've ever seen.

00:48:31.370 --> 00:48:34.400
He's really committed and he keeps coming back.

00:48:34.410 --> 00:48:39.302
This is actually an admission of the commitment of Rasulullah ﷺ

00:48:39.350 --> 00:48:44.590
On the one hand, I will say whatever he's saying is mysteriously magical.

00:48:45.270 --> 00:48:46.330
But it's still a lie,

00:48:46.440 --> 00:48:47.000
and I can't.

00:48:47.370 --> 00:48:48.690
Why does he keep coming back?

00:48:50.070 --> 00:48:51.654
That's (سَٰاحِرٌ كَذَّابٌ)

00:48:52.870 --> 00:48:56.330
Then they said, why can we not accept this magical truth?

00:48:56.340 --> 00:49:01.090
Why do we have to call it a lie? Because he's taking all of our gods

00:49:01.470 --> 00:49:02.700
and turning them into what?

00:49:03.680 --> 00:49:05.000
One God. Now you tell me.

00:49:05.570 --> 00:49:06.700
Look at these two Ayat.

00:49:07.470 --> 00:49:09.590
What did they find strange in the first Ayah?

00:49:11.270 --> 00:49:15.290
What did they find strange in the first Ayah? Only one thing. What was the one thing?

00:49:15.770 --> 00:49:18.290
This is-- that a warner came

00:49:18.670 --> 00:49:21.130
from among themselves. Is it the same in the second Ayah?

00:49:21.230 --> 00:49:22.590
A warner came among themselves?

00:49:23.170 --> 00:49:23.700
Yes,

00:49:24.070 --> 00:49:26.400
but additionally, there are three more things.

00:49:27.570 --> 00:49:30.000
Additionally, there are three more things. One, he's a magician.

00:49:30.970 --> 00:49:32.500
Two he is a perpetual liar.

00:49:32.870 --> 00:49:35.200
Three he took all the gods and made them into

00:49:35.570 --> 00:49:39.590
one. There are three additional things they found strange.

00:49:41.070 --> 00:49:43.200
The Qur'an is so accurate

00:49:44.250 --> 00:49:45.950
that by the end of this sentence,

00:49:45.960 --> 00:49:49.900
Allah recognizes that elsewhere in another Surah entirely

00:49:50.770 --> 00:49:54.300
when they only found one thing strange, this is a strange thing.

00:49:54.310 --> 00:49:57.430
But when they found three more strange things,

00:49:57.530 --> 00:50:01.630
there should be three more expressions that add to the

00:50:01.630 --> 00:50:05.890
strangeness that should be said so (اِنَّ) certainly, this is

00:50:06.260 --> 00:50:08.690
truly (لَشَيْء) truly

00:50:09.260 --> 00:50:12.190
and then (عُجَابٌ) a really strange thing.

00:50:13.160 --> 00:50:18.062
There are three degrees of emphasis in
(إِنَّ هَٰذَا لَشَيْءٌ عُجَابٌ)

00:50:18.060 --> 00:50:21.760
because in that Ayah there are three more things

00:50:21.460 --> 00:50:22.570
that are strange.

00:50:23.960 --> 00:50:28.190
And the Qur'an does this over and over again all over the text.

00:50:29.060 --> 00:50:31.490
Like from a linguistics perspective this is

00:50:33.460 --> 00:50:35.190
either you believe or call it Sihr (سحر).

00:50:37.460 --> 00:50:39.980
You call-- you have to call it magic. I mean, this is I mean,

00:50:40.960 --> 00:50:46.754
how do you keep track of, wait in another Surah revealed two years ago, I said
هَٰذَا لَشَيْءٌ عُجَابٌ

00:50:46.754 --> 00:50:49.590
This time I'm saying three times the more emphasis or

00:50:49.590 --> 00:50:50.950
three times the more things that are strange.

00:50:50.950 --> 00:50:54.642
I should keep track of that. Refer back to that Surah and therefore say, 

00:50:54.712 --> 00:50:56.280
إِنَّ هَٰذَا لَشَيْءٌ عُجَابٌ

00:50:56.660 --> 00:50:57.680
You can't do it.

00:50:58.560 --> 00:50:59.490
You can't keep up.

00:50:59.960 --> 00:51:03.400
I don't even remember what I said five minutes ago. You don't either.

00:51:06.420 --> 00:51:10.080
The Qur'an remembers what it said in one Surah

00:51:10.460 --> 00:51:12.950
and compares it perfectly to another Surah

00:51:12.950 --> 00:51:15.770
if a similar statement comes up and balances them.

00:51:16.560 --> 00:51:17.780
It's beyond explanation,

00:51:18.560 --> 00:51:19.780
Just beyond explanation.